# NOTICE — tos-app-homebridge

This package redistributes the official `homebridge-apt-pkg` release deb
(https://github.com/homebridge/homebridge-apt-pkg), produced by the Homebridge
project and licensed under the Apache License 2.0. The upstream payload —
including the bundled Node.js runtime and all node_modules — ships verbatim;
this repository only adds TOS packaging metadata, a TOS-hardened systemd unit
and documentation.

Deviations from the pipeline's usual conventions (deliberate, documented):

1. Application directory is `/opt/homebridge` (not `/usr/local/homebridge`):
   upstream `start.sh` hardcodes that path, and rebasing 24k files plus
   relative symlinks would risk subtle breakage for zero functional gain.
2. Storage is `/var/lib/homebridge` (upstream convention, cwd-relative).
3. The upstream `lib/systemd/system/homebridge.service` member is replaced by
   a TOS-hardened unit (dedicated `homebridge` system user, sandboxing, UI
   port 18246). The web UI port is changed from upstream's default 8581 to
   18246 via the `platform: config` block seed in config.json (postinst).

Third-party licenses: the bundled Node.js runtime (MIT, see
/opt/homebridge/LICENSE) and npm dependencies (various permissive licenses,
see each package under /opt/homebridge/lib/node_modules and
/var/lib/homebridge/node_modules) keep their upstream license files in place.
